==Trivia==
*Behemoth's Peak's English name may have been intended to foreshadow the addition of the [[:Category:Behemoth Enemies|Behemoth]] type, beginning with the general introduction of [[Ultima Beast Naala]].
**As Naala is the only Behemoth here, the name most likely refers to a mountain peak associated with a singular Behemoth, Naala, not the Behemoth type as a whole.
*According to its Japanese name, [[Silver Current]] refers to a current of water. Since it comes before Ultima Beast Naala, who may represent [[wikipedia:Eikþyrnir|Eikþyrnir]] from Norse mythology, Silver Current could refer to the life-rivers created from the dew that drips from Eikþyrnir's glowing antlers into [[wikipedia:Hvergelmir|Hvergelmir]].
**[[Immortal Zenith]] may correlate or contrast with how Eikþyrnir stands upon one of the afterlife locations, [[wikipedia:Valhalla|Valhalla]], as the stage's Japanese name (天寿を授ける頂 ''Tenju o Sazukeru Itadaki'') can be literally translated as "The Summit That Bestows Natural Lifespans"; 天寿 ''tenju'' consists of the kanji for "heaven" and "longevity" and means one's natural lifespan.

